 "working": "Let S = 1 + 4/3 + 7/9 + ... + (3n-2)/3^(n-1). Then (1/3)S = 1/3 + 4/9 + ... + (3n-5)/3^(n-1) + (3n-2)/3^n. Subtract: (2/3)S = 1 + 3(1/3 + 1/9 + ... + 1/3^(n-1)) - (3n-2)/3^n. The GP sum is (1/2)(1 - 1/3^(n-1)). So (2/3)S = 5/2 - 3/(2*3^(n-1)) - (3n-2)/3^n = 5/2 - (6n+5)/(2*3^n). Multiply by 3/2: S = 15/4 - (6n+5)/(4*3^(n-1)).\n\nIndependent check: The kth term is (3k−2)/3^(k−1). Summing gives Sₙ = 15/4 − (6n+5)/(4·3^(n−1)).",
 "solution": "Let $S_n=1+\\frac43+\\frac79+\\cdots+\\frac{3n-2}{3^{n-1}}$. Subtracting $\\frac13S_n$ from $S_n$ and summing the resulting geometric series gives\n$$\\frac23S_n=\\frac52-\\frac{6n+5}{2\\cdot3^n}.\n$$\nHence $\\displaystyle S_n=\\frac{15}{4}-\\frac{6n+5}{4\\cdot3^{n-1}}$.",
